1
00:00:23,394 --> 00:00:24,796
<i>To my dearest wife.</i>

2
00:00:25,463 --> 00:00:29,400
<i>It's already been a week</i>
<i>since you went back to your parents' home.</i>

3
00:00:29,467 --> 00:00:30,935
<i>How are you doing?</i>

4
00:00:31,002 --> 00:00:32,370
<i>As for me,</i>

5
00:00:32,437 --> 00:00:35,607
<i>things are starting off smoothly</i>
<i>at the new school.</i>

6
00:00:35,673 --> 00:00:38,176
<i>-My class had a truant kid…</i>
-You can't prank people like this!

7
00:00:38,243 --> 00:00:40,078
<i>But thanks to my efforts,</i>

8
00:00:40,145 --> 00:00:42,814
<i>he finally started</i>
<i>coming to class the other day.</i>

9
00:00:42,881 --> 00:00:44,883
Forgive yourself, Kenta.

10
00:00:46,417 --> 00:00:48,453
The only one who can forgive you

11
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:50,021
is you.

12
00:00:50,088 --> 00:00:52,123
I was thinking about
a nickname for myself.

13
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:54,092
Ken-Ken. So call me that!

14
00:00:54,726 --> 00:00:59,430
<i>If things keep going like this,</i>
<i>my feedback scores will keep going up,</i>

15
00:01:00,331 --> 00:01:03,668
<i>and I will for sure get a bonus.</i>

16
00:01:03,735 --> 00:01:06,771
<i>No need to worry anymore,</i>
<i>you can come back home now.</i>

17
00:01:07,505 --> 00:01:09,374
"Please."

18
00:01:09,941 --> 00:01:10,842
Please!

19
00:01:10,909 --> 00:01:12,744
All right, I've got this.

20
00:01:15,446 --> 00:01:16,714
She replied.

21
00:01:17,882 --> 00:01:21,719
SO, DID YOU FIND OUT
WHAT BEING A GREAT TEACHER MEANS?

22
00:01:21,786 --> 00:01:24,122
Oh, that…

23
00:01:25,723 --> 00:01:30,261
NOT YET, SORRY…

24
00:01:30,328 --> 00:01:31,930
I SEE

25
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:36,601
Good morning.

26
00:01:37,235 --> 00:01:38,937
-Good morning.
-Huh?

27
00:01:40,738 --> 00:01:41,873
What?

28
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:43,208
Huh? Oh, good morning?

29
00:01:43,274 --> 00:01:44,342
Good morning.

30
00:01:44,409 --> 00:01:46,110
Good morning.

31
00:01:46,744 --> 00:01:48,813
Hey, is there something on my face?

32
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:51,149
-No.
-Then, did something happen?

33
00:01:51,216 --> 00:01:54,018
I figured, sooner or later,
it would turn out like this.

34
00:01:54,085 --> 00:01:55,553
What do you mean by that?

35
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:58,056
Mr. Onizuka, fight on, don't give up!

36
00:01:58,122 --> 00:02:00,858
But what on earth is going on?

37
00:02:01,526 --> 00:02:02,360
Jeez.

38
00:02:02,427 --> 00:02:03,661
Good morning.

39
00:02:03,728 --> 00:02:05,163
Good morning.

40
00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:06,431
Good morning.

41
00:02:10,702 --> 00:02:12,804
Ms. Kashiwabara, do you know anything?

42
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:15,506
Everyone is looking at me
like they feel sorry for me.

43
00:02:15,573 --> 00:02:18,209
What? Haven't you looked at your tablet?

44
00:02:18,276 --> 00:02:20,445
No, I forgot to take it home yesterday.

45
00:02:28,753 --> 00:02:30,521
What? No way!

46
00:02:30,588 --> 00:02:31,990
This is strange!

47
00:02:32,056 --> 00:02:35,159
With Kenta Katayama back, our class
became a perfect number, so why?

48
00:02:35,226 --> 00:02:38,730
Maybe you were getting cocky,
and the other students got annoyed.

49
00:02:38,796 --> 00:02:40,765
Was I getting cocky?

50
00:02:40,832 --> 00:02:42,433
Yes, quite a bit.

51
00:02:43,735 --> 00:02:45,336
Then you should have told me!

52
00:02:45,403 --> 00:02:48,506
I'm sorry, you looked so happy
that I thought it would be bad to ruin it.

53
00:02:49,674 --> 00:02:50,908
Mr. Onizuka.

54
00:02:51,909 --> 00:02:52,910
Come.

55
00:02:54,078 --> 00:02:55,980
What on earth do you intend to do?

56
00:02:56,047 --> 00:02:59,984
Out of 28 students in Class 1-B,

57
00:03:00,051 --> 00:03:02,654
27 have given you a low rating.

58
00:03:03,788 --> 00:03:06,891
Just for reference,
what's their reason for the low rating?

59
00:03:07,859 --> 00:03:10,128
Even though it's in the school rules,

60
00:03:10,194 --> 00:03:12,664
you don't address students
with honorifics.

61
00:03:12,730 --> 00:03:16,768
Well, I thought we could
get closer that way.

62
00:03:16,834 --> 00:03:19,771
On top of that, you forced students
to make up nicknames.

63
00:03:19,837 --> 00:03:24,175
No, I only suggested using nicknames.

64
00:03:24,242 --> 00:03:27,545
You also told them to eat mystery hotpots,
do tests of courage,

65
00:03:27,612 --> 00:03:28,846
and run towards the sunset?

66
00:03:28,913 --> 00:03:32,717
It's like, "Let's enjoy our youth!"
We all did those things back then, no?

67
00:03:33,284 --> 00:03:34,285
Right, Ryunosuke?

68
00:03:34,352 --> 00:03:37,622
You kind of forced us
to do them, Mr. Onizuka.

69
00:03:37,689 --> 00:03:39,290
Do you seriously think that?

70
00:03:39,357 --> 00:03:41,459
But I was going to say,
it ended up being fun.

71
00:03:41,526 --> 00:03:43,628
-Seriously?
-Anyway…

72
00:03:43,695 --> 00:03:47,432
It's unheard of for a teacher's rating
to drop this quickly

73
00:03:47,498 --> 00:03:51,069
ever since the feedback system started.

74
00:03:51,903 --> 00:03:55,673
At this rate, we'll have no choice
but to have you quit.

75
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:56,708
Right, Principal?

76
00:03:56,774 --> 00:03:59,510
Huh? Well, I suppose so.

77
00:03:59,577 --> 00:04:01,713
Wait a minute, please.

78
00:04:02,213 --> 00:04:04,082
I think I did a decent job.

79
00:04:04,148 --> 00:04:06,984
I promise I'll raise my ratings
and reach the top!

80
00:04:07,785 --> 00:04:08,920
In that case,

81
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:13,057
if by next week you can't get even
one more good rating, you must quit.

82
00:04:13,124 --> 00:04:13,958
Right, Principal?

83
00:04:14,525 --> 00:04:16,294
Well, I suppose so.

84
00:04:16,361 --> 00:04:19,397
W-Wait, are you serious? Give me a break!

85
00:04:20,898 --> 00:04:23,167
Isn't that a bit too harsh?

86
00:04:23,668 --> 00:04:26,204
Mr. Onizuka hasn't been
at our school for very long.

87
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:28,439
-What are you talking about?
-Hey!

88
00:04:29,073 --> 00:04:33,478
You share the responsibility for hiring
such a problematic teacher, Mr. Miyazawa!

89
00:04:33,544 --> 00:04:34,245
No, but…

90
00:04:34,312 --> 00:04:36,047
Besides, school issues

91
00:04:36,114 --> 00:04:40,184
are to be left to the judgment
of myself and the Principal.

92
00:04:40,251 --> 00:04:42,220
Isn't that what your company agreed to?

93
00:04:42,286 --> 00:04:43,621
-You're exactly right.
-Yes.

94
00:04:43,688 --> 00:04:45,323
-Hey.
-Wait.

95
00:04:45,857 --> 00:04:49,193
Please don't fire me.
Implants cost a lot of money…

96
00:04:50,027 --> 00:04:51,629
And my wife is leaving me…

97
00:04:51,696 --> 00:04:54,699
I don't give a damn
about your personal matters!

98
00:06:20,618 --> 00:06:23,087
It hurts! My tooth aches again!

99
00:06:23,855 --> 00:06:25,990
But seriously, those kids…

100
00:06:26,057 --> 00:06:29,760
Instead of writing things on this,
just tell me directly.

101
00:06:29,827 --> 00:06:32,029
By not drawing a line in the sand,

102
00:06:32,096 --> 00:06:34,298
we are allowing kids these days
to walk all over us.

103
00:06:34,365 --> 00:06:36,734
If you say that,
you'll be out of here in no time.

104
00:06:36,801 --> 00:06:38,970
What am I supposed to do then?

105
00:06:39,036 --> 00:06:41,572
Just do what you want to do, Mr. Onizuka.

106
00:06:41,639 --> 00:06:44,609
There you go again,
abandoning people like that.

107
00:06:45,409 --> 00:06:46,944
Good morning.

108
00:06:47,945 --> 00:06:49,547
Good morning.

109
00:06:56,187 --> 00:07:00,224
Today, there is something
I want to clear up with all of you.

110
00:07:05,863 --> 00:07:09,166
It seems there was some misunderstanding.

111
00:07:09,233 --> 00:07:13,971
When I said let's use nicknames,
I just meant you could, if you wanted to.

112
00:07:14,038 --> 00:07:15,039
Okay?

113
00:07:16,641 --> 00:07:20,678
Just like Ms. Ayano said the other day,

114
00:07:20,745 --> 00:07:23,781
nicknames carry the risk
of leading to bullying,

115
00:07:23,848 --> 00:07:27,818
and students who wish to be addressed
with honorifics may also do that, so…

116
00:07:28,452 --> 00:07:30,688
-Flexibility.
-That's right!

117
00:07:30,755 --> 00:07:32,790
As you get older, words fail you.

118
00:07:32,857 --> 00:07:37,962
Anyway, if things stay like this,
my wife is going to get mad at me.

119
00:07:38,029 --> 00:07:41,332
So if I could somehow get a good rating…

120
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:44,535
You're quite laid-back,
for an ex-bike gang member.

121
00:07:44,602 --> 00:07:47,838
You look so cool,
yet you're scared of your wife.

122
00:07:50,508 --> 00:07:51,676
That's why…

123
00:07:52,610 --> 00:07:55,780
I'll work hard for your sake.

124
00:07:55,846 --> 00:07:58,282
So if there's anything
I can do, just let me know.

125
00:07:58,849 --> 00:08:02,553
Even if it's something embarrassing
that you can't tell others, I'll do it.

126
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:03,688
Is that true?

127
00:08:05,656 --> 00:08:09,994
Is there something
you want to request, Ms. Ayano?

128
00:08:11,095 --> 00:08:15,166
Never mind. If anything happens,
I'll just consult the AI.

129
00:08:15,232 --> 00:08:17,168
-What?
-'Preciate it!

130
00:08:17,735 --> 00:08:18,502
'Preciate?

131
00:08:18,569 --> 00:08:20,972
I appreciate the thought, but no thanks.

132
00:08:27,411 --> 00:08:30,881
You kids, always treating people like…

133
00:08:33,718 --> 00:08:37,755
Um, Ms. Kashiwabara, please say something.

134
00:08:37,822 --> 00:08:39,223
Please don't pass it off to me.

135
00:08:39,290 --> 00:08:41,625
Don't say that,
you're the assistant teacher!

136
00:08:41,692 --> 00:08:45,196
For now, you better wrap this up quick,
or homeroom will end.

137
00:08:45,262 --> 00:08:47,331
-Well…
-Onicchi.

138
00:08:47,832 --> 00:08:49,600
Please do something.

139
00:08:50,101 --> 00:08:51,569
Please.

140
00:09:05,583 --> 00:09:07,618
What are you doing, Onicchi?

141
00:09:08,886 --> 00:09:10,321
How pathetic.

142
00:09:10,388 --> 00:09:13,257
Calling me that doesn't change anything…

143
00:09:13,324 --> 00:09:14,859
Jeez.

144
00:09:14,925 --> 00:09:17,161
Maybe I'll put in a low rating too.

145
00:09:17,662 --> 00:09:21,232
Hey, don't do that, Ken-Ken.

146
00:09:32,543 --> 00:09:34,278
I knew you'd be here.

147
00:09:35,613 --> 00:09:37,481
Leave me alone, Ryunosuke.

148
00:09:38,215 --> 00:09:42,353
At this rate, it looks like I'm going
to get low ratings from all 28 students.

149
00:09:43,521 --> 00:09:45,723
Stop saying such pathetic things.

150
00:09:46,590 --> 00:09:48,059
Look at this.

151
00:09:50,361 --> 00:09:51,195
What?

152
00:09:51,262 --> 00:09:52,196
What's this?

153
00:09:52,263 --> 00:09:55,166
Since your rating dropped
so suddenly, I looked into it.

154
00:09:55,232 --> 00:09:58,035
It seems like after someone
in Class 1-B typed this in,

155
00:09:58,102 --> 00:10:00,137
the low ratings spread.

156
00:10:00,204 --> 00:10:01,272
What?

157
00:10:01,338 --> 00:10:05,242
When the previous teacher quit, something
similar happened, so I was curious.

158
00:10:06,043 --> 00:10:08,245
-Then should we find this culprit?
-What?

159
00:10:08,312 --> 00:10:11,248
I think if you do that,
it'll only get you more resentment.

160
00:10:11,315 --> 00:10:12,349
Then what do I do?

161
00:10:12,917 --> 00:10:16,721
For now, why don't you just try
to raise your rating?

162
00:10:16,787 --> 00:10:17,788
How?

163
00:10:17,855 --> 00:10:19,757
Well, about that…

164
00:10:21,092 --> 00:10:24,361
Why not try asking other teachers?

165
00:10:24,428 --> 00:10:26,464
You might find some good ideas.

166
00:10:27,298 --> 00:10:31,902
So this "that" is talking about
the sentence from here to here.

167
00:10:32,903 --> 00:10:34,238
I get it now!

168
00:10:39,777 --> 00:10:41,078
Thank you very much.

169
00:10:47,218 --> 00:10:48,886
Ms. Koizumi.

170
00:10:48,953 --> 00:10:51,822
You were called
a "Great Teacher" just now.

171
00:10:51,889 --> 00:10:54,158
Why is that? Please tell me your secret.

172
00:10:54,225 --> 00:10:55,526
What?

173
00:10:55,593 --> 00:10:56,627
Well…

174
00:10:56,694 --> 00:11:02,466
I'm just "going my way,"
but the other day, a student in my class

175
00:11:02,533 --> 00:11:05,636
told me that compared to other teachers,
my class is super fun!

176
00:11:05,703 --> 00:11:09,507
And that they feel lucky
they have me as a homeroom teacher.

177
00:11:09,573 --> 00:11:11,208
And you know, the other day…

178
00:11:11,275 --> 00:11:12,910
A student asked,

179
00:11:12,977 --> 00:11:16,313
"Miss, did you use to be a model?"

180
00:11:18,249 --> 00:11:20,551
-Is what I told them!
-That's amazing.

181
00:11:20,618 --> 00:11:21,819
I wasn't a model.

182
00:11:22,386 --> 00:11:24,722
She's just bragging. Not helpful at all.

183
00:11:26,590 --> 00:11:29,794
Mr. Abe. Why are you so popular?

184
00:11:30,494 --> 00:11:33,164
On closer look, you are
quite handsome, actually.

185
00:11:33,230 --> 00:11:37,735
I utilize ICT and emphasize active
learning where students participate

186
00:11:37,802 --> 00:11:41,438
in a proactive way, to draw out
their abilities, interests, and concerns.

187
00:11:41,505 --> 00:11:44,175
In the coming era, interactive learning

188
00:11:44,241 --> 00:11:48,379
that uses tablets, like at our school,
and two-way learning will be mainstr--

189
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:50,581
Are you listening?

190
00:11:50,648 --> 00:11:51,482
Yes.

191
00:11:51,549 --> 00:11:54,351
Lately, maybe because of my age,
I haven't been able to sleep.

192
00:12:01,025 --> 00:12:02,393
Mr. Yamamura.

193
00:12:04,695 --> 00:12:05,863
It's Murayama.

194
00:12:05,930 --> 00:12:08,265
Sorry, Mr. Murayama.

195
00:12:09,166 --> 00:12:10,134
What is it?

196
00:12:10,201 --> 00:12:11,435
Um, well…

197
00:12:13,637 --> 00:12:15,706
Actually, nevermind.

198
00:12:17,508 --> 00:12:19,009
Found anything helpful?

199
00:12:19,076 --> 00:12:20,511
Not at all.

200
00:12:21,745 --> 00:12:25,216
Ms. Kashiwabara, what would you do
if you got a low rating?

201
00:12:25,282 --> 00:12:27,351
-Nothing in particular.
-Why?

202
00:12:27,418 --> 00:12:30,487
I plan to leave this job someday,
once I find a good company.

203
00:12:30,554 --> 00:12:31,222
What?

204
00:12:31,288 --> 00:12:34,925
I got into this school because
I happen to have a teaching license.

205
00:12:34,992 --> 00:12:36,527
I thought if things went well,

206
00:12:36,594 --> 00:12:39,263
I might get recruited by the company
that runs this place.

207
00:12:39,330 --> 00:12:41,198
That is…

208
00:12:41,265 --> 00:12:44,168
-What? You have a problem?
-No…

209
00:12:44,235 --> 00:12:46,070
I have a lot of things I want to say…

210
00:12:46,136 --> 00:12:49,573
But right now my hands are full
with my own problems, so let's leave it.

211
00:12:57,448 --> 00:12:58,549
It's no use.

212
00:12:59,383 --> 00:13:02,653
I can't find a breakthrough at all.

213
00:13:07,224 --> 00:13:08,859
What's wrong, Ms. Yuu?

214
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:10,594
Teacher.

215
00:13:10,661 --> 00:13:11,495
Yes?

216
00:13:11,562 --> 00:13:15,766
If you listen to my request,
I'll give you a good rating.

217
00:13:17,568 --> 00:13:18,469
Really?

218
00:13:19,136 --> 00:13:22,072
You'll really do it, no matter
how embarrassing, right?

219
00:13:22,907 --> 00:13:24,608
Of course.

220
00:13:25,743 --> 00:13:26,744
So what is it?

221
00:13:30,214 --> 00:13:31,916
I want to start a Precision Drill Team!

222
00:13:32,983 --> 00:13:34,051
Oh!

223
00:13:34,118 --> 00:13:35,719
Okay, I see.

224
00:13:35,786 --> 00:13:37,288
Have you not heard of them?

225
00:13:37,354 --> 00:13:39,056
Of course I have!

226
00:13:39,123 --> 00:13:41,558
The loser is forced
to do something unpleasant, right?

227
00:13:41,625 --> 00:13:43,294
That's a penalty drill!

228
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:44,962
This is a Drill Team.

229
00:13:49,767 --> 00:13:51,669
Oh, I see.

230
00:13:52,303 --> 00:13:55,272
I did this at some school a long time ago.

231
00:13:55,339 --> 00:13:56,674
Then you understand, right?

232
00:13:57,241 --> 00:14:00,377
Drill Teams can express
a sense of solidarity,

233
00:14:00,444 --> 00:14:03,514
and they don't require
any real skills, anyone can do it.

234
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:06,183
Sounds good. Do it. I'll be the advisor.

235
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:08,252
Could you not make it sound so easy?

236
00:14:08,986 --> 00:14:09,887
Why?

237
00:14:10,387 --> 00:14:13,691
I don't think anyone in our school
would do it with me,

238
00:14:13,757 --> 00:14:15,960
and people would just say it's a hassle.

239
00:14:16,026 --> 00:14:16,961
No way.

240
00:14:17,027 --> 00:14:21,332
Way! Back in middle school,
people told me that, so I gave up.

241
00:14:23,067 --> 00:14:25,302
What do you want me to do?

242
00:14:27,137 --> 00:14:29,206
During homeroom, could you say,

243
00:14:29,273 --> 00:14:33,577
"Hey, everyone, Drill Teams look fun,
so why don't you make one?"

244
00:14:33,644 --> 00:14:35,279
Just make the suggestion.

245
00:14:35,346 --> 00:14:39,116
Of course, nobody will raise their hand,
so you'll force me to do it.

246
00:14:39,950 --> 00:14:42,853
You'll say, "You be the team leader!"

247
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:47,825
And I'll say,
"What? No way! I can't do it!"

248
00:14:47,891 --> 00:14:50,694
Basically, like I don't want to do it.

249
00:14:51,362 --> 00:14:53,097
You want me to put on an act?

250
00:14:53,163 --> 00:14:54,765
It'll be fine!

251
00:14:54,832 --> 00:14:57,701
After that, I'll be like,
"I was doing it reluctantly,

252
00:14:57,768 --> 00:15:00,771
but it's actually pretty fun,"
and draw people in that way.

253
00:15:02,439 --> 00:15:04,408
No, that's weird.

254
00:15:04,475 --> 00:15:06,210
You're the one who wants to do it, right?

255
00:15:09,279 --> 00:15:10,347
What?

256
00:15:11,048 --> 00:15:11,882
Fine then.

257
00:15:11,949 --> 00:15:14,151
All right! I'll do it!

258
00:15:17,454 --> 00:15:18,522
Okay.

259
00:15:22,092 --> 00:15:22,760
CLASS 1-B

260
00:15:22,826 --> 00:15:24,094
Today…

261
00:15:24,161 --> 00:15:24,995
I…

262
00:15:25,629 --> 00:15:29,066
I mean, I have a proposal for you all.

263
00:15:33,470 --> 00:15:35,372
How do you use this?

264
00:15:35,439 --> 00:15:36,673
The screen?

265
00:15:37,241 --> 00:15:37,908
Yes.

266
00:15:38,876 --> 00:15:41,612
-Like this.
-Oh, I see.

267
00:15:46,884 --> 00:15:47,885
Well…

268
00:15:47,951 --> 00:15:50,888
How do I play this video…

269
00:15:50,954 --> 00:15:51,789
Press here.

270
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:53,824
Thanks.

271
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:59,096
This is… a Drill Team.

272
00:15:59,163 --> 00:16:00,297
We know.

273
00:16:01,165 --> 00:16:01,999
Is that so?

274
00:16:02,066 --> 00:16:04,301
-I've seen videos of them.
-Me too.

275
00:16:04,368 --> 00:16:06,937
Okay, then this will be quick.

276
00:16:09,106 --> 00:16:13,177
It looks incredibly fun, so I thought
it would be great if we made a team.

277
00:16:18,282 --> 00:16:20,951
Is there anyone who wants to do it?

278
00:16:21,018 --> 00:16:21,952
Yes?

279
00:16:28,492 --> 00:16:30,594
Can't be helped then.

280
00:16:30,661 --> 00:16:33,964
I'm going to decide
the team leader myself!

281
00:16:34,531 --> 00:16:38,502
Who would be a good candidate?

282
00:16:39,336 --> 00:16:40,838
I'll do it.

283
00:16:40,904 --> 00:16:42,806
Huh? Ken-Ken?

284
00:16:43,607 --> 00:16:46,243
-You want to do it?
-Yeah. It looks fun.

285
00:16:47,111 --> 00:16:50,147
Look, isn't that great? Ken-Ken is in!

286
00:16:54,017 --> 00:16:55,219
What?

287
00:16:55,285 --> 00:16:58,755
Why are you telling me that?
I don't get it at all!

288
00:16:58,822 --> 00:17:01,692
No, sorry, I'm sorry.
I thought you might like it too.

289
00:17:01,758 --> 00:17:04,294
You can't do it alone, right?
Why not join Ken-Ken?

290
00:17:04,361 --> 00:17:06,730
No, wait a minute. This is such a pain.

291
00:17:08,699 --> 00:17:10,767
Seriously, I can't believe it.

292
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:19,042
So, how did I do?

293
00:17:19,109 --> 00:17:21,044
Mr. Onizuka, your acting is way too bad.

294
00:17:21,111 --> 00:17:23,580
I was so scared I would get exposed.

295
00:17:23,647 --> 00:17:24,548
Sorry.

296
00:17:25,215 --> 00:17:27,951
So you'll give me a high rating, right?

297
00:17:29,019 --> 00:17:31,622
What are you talking about?
There's still more to do.

298
00:17:31,688 --> 00:17:33,323
What? Why?

299
00:17:34,091 --> 00:17:36,760
If the school doesn't approve it,
we can't form a team.

300
00:17:36,827 --> 00:17:38,996
You have to convince
the Principal and the Vice Principal.

301
00:17:39,062 --> 00:17:42,366
What? I have to do that too?

302
00:17:42,432 --> 00:17:45,002
Of course. You're the advisor, after all.

303
00:17:46,537 --> 00:17:47,504
Okay.

304
00:17:52,776 --> 00:17:55,312
I see. So that's how it is.

305
00:17:55,379 --> 00:17:57,447
You startled me. What do you want?

306
00:17:57,514 --> 00:18:00,050
I thought his acting smelled a bit fishy.

307
00:18:00,717 --> 00:18:02,286
And if I remember correctly,

308
00:18:02,352 --> 00:18:05,556
back in middle school,
you said you liked Drill Teams.

309
00:18:05,622 --> 00:18:07,558
Don't talk like you know me!

310
00:18:07,624 --> 00:18:10,427
You barely even came to school
back then anyway.

311
00:18:13,096 --> 00:18:15,499
Don't worry. I won't tell anyone.

312
00:18:15,566 --> 00:18:17,534
But shouldn't we practice soon?

313
00:18:21,071 --> 00:18:23,674
All right, for now,
first is how to walk in the march.

314
00:18:29,846 --> 00:18:31,215
Wait, what are you doing?

315
00:18:31,782 --> 00:18:33,650
Your hands shouldn't match your strides.

316
00:18:33,717 --> 00:18:35,018
I know that.

317
00:18:35,085 --> 00:18:38,222
Come on, puff out your chest.
Swing your arms wide.

318
00:18:38,288 --> 00:18:39,323
Okay!

319
00:18:39,957 --> 00:18:41,858
And keep a smile on your face.

320
00:18:43,727 --> 00:18:45,963
You've synced your hands and feet again.

321
00:18:46,597 --> 00:18:48,498
Why is your sense of rhythm so bad?

322
00:18:49,066 --> 00:18:50,067
Shut up.

323
00:18:50,133 --> 00:18:52,903
It's because you suck
at teaching. Show me the video.

324
00:18:54,204 --> 00:18:55,038
Here.

325
00:18:56,940 --> 00:19:00,244
Oh, I see. Something like this, right?

326
00:19:01,144 --> 00:19:02,012
Hey.

327
00:19:02,879 --> 00:19:03,847
What?

328
00:19:04,414 --> 00:19:06,350
Why did you feel like coming to school?

329
00:19:08,986 --> 00:19:13,023
Onicchi said he'd be sad if I died.

330
00:19:14,024 --> 00:19:16,693
I would be sad.

331
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:19,896
<i>Besides, Onicchi is just really warm.</i>

332
00:19:20,497 --> 00:19:21,665
<i>I thought,</i>

333
00:19:22,366 --> 00:19:24,801
maybe this is a person I can trust.

334
00:19:27,537 --> 00:19:28,472
PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE

335
00:19:28,538 --> 00:19:32,943
So that's the situation, I hope
you can approve the Drill Team.

336
00:19:33,010 --> 00:19:35,345
By the way, he is the team leader…

337
00:19:35,412 --> 00:19:36,780
Impossible. Declined.

338
00:19:37,347 --> 00:19:38,148
Why?

339
00:19:39,383 --> 00:19:41,018
Let me ask you instead,

340
00:19:41,084 --> 00:19:45,022
this is neither gymnastics nor dancing,
and it is so easy that anyone can do it.

341
00:19:45,088 --> 00:19:48,225
So why do we have to do it
at all, right, Principal?

342
00:19:48,292 --> 00:19:50,627
-No, but…
-What are you talking about?

343
00:19:50,694 --> 00:19:53,063
Isn't it fun because anyone can do it?

344
00:19:53,130 --> 00:19:55,299
If you want to move that much,
join the Dance Club.

345
00:19:55,365 --> 00:19:58,502
I did join
right after entering our school.

346
00:19:58,568 --> 00:19:59,903
But they made fun of me.

347
00:19:59,970 --> 00:20:02,506
They said I was too incompetent.

348
00:20:03,340 --> 00:20:06,810
But I want people
who aren't good at dancing

349
00:20:06,877 --> 00:20:10,113
to also know the joy of cooperating
and coming together as one.

350
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:14,384
Even if you say that… Right, Principal?

351
00:20:15,085 --> 00:20:18,588
I don't even know who your team leader is.

352
00:20:18,655 --> 00:20:19,890
How about…

353
00:20:20,657 --> 00:20:24,194
we have them gather team members first?

354
00:20:24,861 --> 00:20:28,398
There is a rule that a club
must have at least five members.

355
00:20:28,465 --> 00:20:30,801
PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE

356
00:20:30,867 --> 00:20:32,135
Hey!

357
00:20:32,202 --> 00:20:36,039
Now we just have
to gather five people in total.

358
00:20:36,106 --> 00:20:37,808
Then, please do.

359
00:20:37,874 --> 00:20:38,942
What?

360
00:20:39,009 --> 00:20:40,477
I have to do that too?

361
00:20:41,044 --> 00:20:41,945
What?

362
00:20:42,579 --> 00:20:44,348
Do you want your good feedback?

363
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:47,584
I want it.

364
00:20:48,151 --> 00:20:50,420
Won't you join the Drill Team?

365
00:20:50,487 --> 00:20:54,324
Try it, it's incredibly fun.
Anyone can do it easily.

366
00:20:54,391 --> 00:20:55,592
Please, the Drill Team.

367
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:57,661
The Drill Team.

368
00:20:57,728 --> 00:20:59,429
You're working hard, Onicchi.

369
00:21:00,897 --> 00:21:03,900
But man, that's messy handwriting.

370
00:21:03,967 --> 00:21:05,268
What's this drawing?

371
00:21:05,335 --> 00:21:09,906
Don't say that, help me out. This is even
tougher than that tissue-distributing job!

372
00:21:09,973 --> 00:21:13,510
Come on. Shouting "Drill Team" here
won't get anyone interested.

373
00:21:13,577 --> 00:21:15,278
Then what am I supposed to do?

374
00:21:15,345 --> 00:21:16,880
Promote it.

375
00:21:16,947 --> 00:21:17,814
What?

376
00:21:22,319 --> 00:21:25,355
Everyone, won't you do drills with us?

377
00:21:25,422 --> 00:21:27,657
It helps with dieting too. It's the best!

378
00:21:28,892 --> 00:21:30,193
Wait, what is that?

379
00:21:32,362 --> 00:21:34,264
Those two aren't synchronized at all.

380
00:21:34,331 --> 00:21:35,932
Weirdos.

381
00:21:35,999 --> 00:21:38,735
Ms. Ito, are you really joining them?

382
00:21:39,836 --> 00:21:43,740
I guess I can't do it, after all.
It's such a pain.

383
00:21:43,807 --> 00:21:45,208
Yuu, just quit already.

384
00:21:45,275 --> 00:21:46,643
Just quit.

385
00:21:46,710 --> 00:21:48,812
-You can't do it.
-Totally!

386
00:21:48,879 --> 00:21:50,180
Yeah, you're right.

387
00:21:55,886 --> 00:21:56,787
I'm leaving now.

388
00:21:56,853 --> 00:21:58,221
-Hey!
-It's really fun, you know.

389
00:21:58,288 --> 00:22:01,458
Ms. Kashiwabara, help us out!

390
00:22:01,525 --> 00:22:04,628
I'm sorry. My policy is to not
get involved with club activities.

391
00:22:04,694 --> 00:22:06,163
Why is that?

392
00:22:06,229 --> 00:22:09,399
Guiding club activities is nothing
but a burden for teachers,

393
00:22:09,466 --> 00:22:12,235
and we have to come in
after school and on days off too.

394
00:22:12,302 --> 00:22:14,905
More and more schools
are hiring outside advisors.

395
00:22:14,971 --> 00:22:17,073
Well, that may be true, but…

396
00:22:17,140 --> 00:22:17,974
Besides…

397
00:22:18,041 --> 00:22:21,812
Many students see club activities
as nothing but a distraction.

398
00:22:21,878 --> 00:22:24,214
What's important is exams and the future.

399
00:22:24,281 --> 00:22:26,416
What? Is that true?

400
00:22:27,918 --> 00:22:30,720
Also, this may be
none of my business, but…

401
00:22:30,787 --> 00:22:33,590
This shows favoritism,
so you should stop it.

402
00:22:37,127 --> 00:22:38,462
I'm sorry.

403
00:22:39,362 --> 00:22:40,764
What do you mean?

404
00:22:43,033 --> 00:22:45,969
It seems like I can't help you
any further.

405
00:22:46,036 --> 00:22:49,005
What's that? You said you'd do anything!

406
00:22:49,072 --> 00:22:51,541
You're the one
who wanted to start the team.

407
00:22:51,608 --> 00:22:54,444
Why don't you try
telling the class, honestly?

408
00:22:54,511 --> 00:22:56,379
You understand, don't you?

409
00:22:56,446 --> 00:22:59,182
With the atmosphere in class,
there's no way I can say it.

410
00:23:01,485 --> 00:23:02,652
Come here for a second.

411
00:23:03,286 --> 00:23:04,120
What?

412
00:23:08,158 --> 00:23:11,528
Wait, what on earth are you doing?

413
00:23:11,595 --> 00:23:14,397
Come on. Let go of me!

414
00:23:21,371 --> 00:23:23,907
That guy is working hard every single day.

415
00:23:23,974 --> 00:23:25,775
He wants to get better quickly

416
00:23:26,710 --> 00:23:29,179
and perform together with you, Yuu.

417
00:23:30,814 --> 00:23:32,115
Damn it!

418
00:23:34,117 --> 00:23:37,287
You're the leader
of the Drill Team, aren't you?

419
00:23:37,354 --> 00:23:41,258
What good is a leader who is ashamed
of what they want to do?

420
00:23:41,858 --> 00:23:45,462
A person like that
can never inspire people.

421
00:23:46,363 --> 00:23:48,565
Hey, Ken-Ken! Working hard, huh?

422
00:23:48,632 --> 00:23:50,667
-Oh, Onicchi.
-Okay, let's do this.

423
00:23:51,234 --> 00:23:52,736
-Let's go.
-All right.

424
00:23:52,802 --> 00:23:55,639
-One, two.
-One, two… Huh?

425
00:23:56,239 --> 00:23:58,441
You're as bad as always, Onicchi.

426
00:23:58,508 --> 00:24:00,176
Shut up, I'm better than you.

427
00:24:00,243 --> 00:24:01,077
Ready, go.

428
00:24:01,144 --> 00:24:02,846
One, two.

429
00:24:02,913 --> 00:24:04,781
CLASS 1-B

430
00:24:08,451 --> 00:24:09,753
Where should we eat?

431
00:24:11,788 --> 00:24:13,056
In the lounge?

432
00:24:17,093 --> 00:24:18,295
Everyone!

433
00:24:19,195 --> 00:24:21,164
Could you listen to me for a moment?

434
00:24:26,036 --> 00:24:27,070
Actually…

435
00:24:28,338 --> 00:24:29,839
It's about the Drill Team.

436
00:24:30,540 --> 00:24:32,709
I was the one who really wanted to do it.

437
00:24:32,776 --> 00:24:35,612
But I didn't have the courage to tell
everyone about making one,

438
00:24:36,379 --> 00:24:40,250
so I asked Mr. Onizuka
to put on that bad act.

439
00:24:41,418 --> 00:24:42,519
So…

440
00:24:45,255 --> 00:24:47,624
Why do you want
to form a team so badly, anyway?

441
00:24:50,627 --> 00:24:51,761
I…

442
00:24:52,696 --> 00:24:55,732
When I was in middle school,
I didn't do any club activities,

443
00:24:55,799 --> 00:24:58,268
and couldn't make any friends at all.

444
00:25:00,670 --> 00:25:01,905
But one girl…

445
00:25:02,706 --> 00:25:05,609
She invited me to try it with her.

446
00:25:06,176 --> 00:25:09,946
At first, I thought it was super lame,

447
00:25:11,548 --> 00:25:14,050
but when I tried it, it was so much fun,

448
00:25:14,751 --> 00:25:17,520
and for the first time in my life,
I made a best friend.

449
00:25:18,288 --> 00:25:19,723
I was so happy.

450
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:26,463
That's why we promised when we went to
high school, we would try to make a team.

451
00:25:27,897 --> 00:25:30,066
But we went to different schools.

452
00:25:32,369 --> 00:25:35,372
I couldn't be with her anymore…

453
00:25:38,541 --> 00:25:42,312
I thought, maybe I should give up.

454
00:25:43,847 --> 00:25:47,684
But then I heard my best friend started
a team at her high school,

455
00:25:48,852 --> 00:25:51,087
and I figured I couldn't lose.

456
00:25:53,690 --> 00:25:55,425
It's embarrassing, but…

457
00:25:56,259 --> 00:26:00,330
My dream is to form a team
with everyone in this class.

458
00:26:00,997 --> 00:26:03,033
If there's anyone who wants some friends,

459
00:26:03,900 --> 00:26:06,403
like me back in middle school…

460
00:26:06,469 --> 00:26:08,805
Won't you do it with me?

461
00:26:09,639 --> 00:26:11,007
Please.

462
00:26:19,182 --> 00:26:20,050
Are you done?

463
00:26:21,251 --> 00:26:22,085
What?

464
00:26:22,652 --> 00:26:25,722
Sorry, I'm starving.

465
00:26:26,656 --> 00:26:28,792
If I don't hurry,
the melon bread will sell out.

466
00:26:33,329 --> 00:26:34,497
I'm sorry.

467
00:26:34,564 --> 00:26:37,600
I want to help, but I've got no time
because of cram school.

468
00:26:38,435 --> 00:26:41,638
-Yeah.
-But I'll cheer you on. Good luck.

469
00:26:43,206 --> 00:26:44,374
Thank you.

470
00:26:59,089 --> 00:27:00,957
Won't you join the Drill Team?

471
00:27:01,024 --> 00:27:02,892
LOOKING FOR DRILL TEAM MEMBERS!

472
00:27:06,463 --> 00:27:10,467
Don't worry about it.
I'm sure someone will do it with us.

473
00:27:12,135 --> 00:27:13,403
Do you think so?

474
00:27:13,470 --> 00:27:16,272
We even have this
gorgeous signboard I made.

475
00:27:16,339 --> 00:27:17,173
LOOKING FOR MEMBERS

476
00:27:18,441 --> 00:27:19,676
So weird.

477
00:27:21,811 --> 00:27:25,482
DRILL TEAM

478
00:27:33,223 --> 00:27:34,357
You see…

479
00:27:35,125 --> 00:27:37,627
I realized something
when I joined the Dance Club.

480
00:27:38,228 --> 00:27:41,397
It's impossible for me to dance like that.

481
00:27:41,464 --> 00:27:43,967
But I like moving my body.

482
00:27:44,667 --> 00:27:46,603
And it's not like
I'm good at other things,

483
00:27:47,203 --> 00:27:49,072
like studying or music…

484
00:27:53,610 --> 00:27:55,912
Won't you join the Drill Team?

485
00:27:55,979 --> 00:27:57,947
-Please.
-Please.

486
00:27:58,014 --> 00:28:00,483
-Won't you join the Drill Team?
-Join us!

487
00:28:00,550 --> 00:28:02,418
Won't you join the Drill Team?

488
00:28:04,320 --> 00:28:05,755
Thank you very much.

489
00:28:05,822 --> 00:28:08,158
The Drill Team, huh?

490
00:28:08,224 --> 00:28:11,294
Looks kind of good. Maybe I'll join.

491
00:28:11,361 --> 00:28:12,529
Really?

492
00:28:13,096 --> 00:28:14,564
But can guys like us do it?

493
00:28:14,631 --> 00:28:16,866
It's fine. It's easy.

494
00:28:17,433 --> 00:28:19,502
Then, will you give us a lesson?

495
00:28:21,304 --> 00:28:22,138
Yes.

496
00:28:24,641 --> 00:28:26,442
Then, shall we give it a try?

497
00:28:26,509 --> 00:28:29,112
-I'll turn on the music.
-Sorry, not you.

498
00:28:29,179 --> 00:28:30,346
What?

499
00:28:30,413 --> 00:28:33,750
We want to be taught by her.

500
00:28:36,219 --> 00:28:37,720
But it's better if everyone
does it together--

501
00:28:37,787 --> 00:28:39,789
If you don't want to, we can quit.

502
00:28:43,226 --> 00:28:44,360
Fine.

503
00:28:55,638 --> 00:28:57,874
Then, we'll start
with the basic way of walking.

504
00:28:57,941 --> 00:29:01,878
Chest out, big arm movements,
and a smile on your face.

505
00:29:02,912 --> 00:29:04,080
Like this?

506
00:29:04,647 --> 00:29:05,648
Yes.

507
00:29:05,715 --> 00:29:07,517
-Yay!
-There we go!

508
00:29:07,584 --> 00:29:10,220
We just spin around like this, right?

509
00:29:10,286 --> 00:29:11,654
That's true, but…

510
00:29:13,489 --> 00:29:15,124
Sorry, please stop!

511
00:29:15,191 --> 00:29:17,393
-Why?
-I'm telling you, stop!

512
00:29:17,460 --> 00:29:19,529
-Hey!
-Got you!

513
00:29:19,596 --> 00:29:20,630
Stop it!

514
00:29:22,832 --> 00:29:23,666
Oh!

515
00:29:23,733 --> 00:29:26,336
Looks like things are heating up.

516
00:29:28,037 --> 00:29:29,205
Let me…

517
00:29:30,039 --> 00:29:31,541
join too!

518
00:29:34,377 --> 00:29:35,178
What?

519
00:29:39,916 --> 00:29:41,284
Hey! Let go!

520
00:29:41,351 --> 00:29:42,585
Ken-Ken!

521
00:29:45,321 --> 00:29:46,956
-Okay!
-Ouch…

522
00:29:52,161 --> 00:29:55,298
-Let go! Hey!
-That hurts!

523
00:29:57,567 --> 00:29:59,869
Why? Isn't this fun?

524
00:29:59,936 --> 00:30:01,371
Whoa!

525
00:30:01,437 --> 00:30:03,573
-It hurts…
-Let me tell you.

526
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:06,242
If you pull any weird tricks
on my students…

527
00:30:06,309 --> 00:30:08,444
I'll make you do drills all night long!

528
00:30:08,511 --> 00:30:11,347
-Let go!
-Please let go!

529
00:30:13,549 --> 00:30:14,517
Run along.

530
00:30:20,556 --> 00:30:22,492
Are you okay, Yuu?

531
00:30:24,527 --> 00:30:25,762
I'm quitting.

532
00:30:26,329 --> 00:30:27,163
What?

533
00:30:27,664 --> 00:30:28,564
The Drill Team?

534
00:30:29,198 --> 00:30:30,400
This school.

535
00:30:31,501 --> 00:30:32,368
What?

536
00:30:32,435 --> 00:30:34,270
I'm going to take a year off,

537
00:30:34,337 --> 00:30:38,107
take the exam for the school my best
friend went to, and join the club there.

538
00:30:38,174 --> 00:30:41,277
Wait! Are you serious?

539
00:30:42,912 --> 00:30:44,981
I shouldn't have come
to a school like this!

540
00:30:49,953 --> 00:30:52,121
What are you going to do, Onicchi?

541
00:30:52,188 --> 00:30:53,156
Well…

542
00:30:54,490 --> 00:30:56,159
I'm not sure.

543
00:30:57,093 --> 00:31:00,296
Things took quite a left turn.

544
00:31:05,101 --> 00:31:07,537
STAFF ROOM

545
00:31:07,603 --> 00:31:09,505
"Are you okay?

546
00:31:09,572 --> 00:31:10,840
Yuu."

547
00:31:11,341 --> 00:31:16,179
"Come to school, I'll be waiting."

548
00:31:16,245 --> 00:31:17,113
Yeah.

549
00:31:17,180 --> 00:31:18,614
Good morning.

550
00:31:18,681 --> 00:31:20,249
Good morning.

551
00:31:21,484 --> 00:31:24,754
I heard Ms. Ito Yuu
is withdrawing from our school.

552
00:31:24,821 --> 00:31:25,822
No…

553
00:31:25,888 --> 00:31:29,292
That's just what she's saying, there's no
way her parents will accept it.

554
00:31:29,359 --> 00:31:31,461
It seems they did accept it.

555
00:31:32,028 --> 00:31:33,596
What? No way?

556
00:31:34,397 --> 00:31:35,732
Mr. Onizuka.

557
00:31:40,236 --> 00:31:41,804
Look at this.

558
00:31:45,208 --> 00:31:46,309
Seriously?

559
00:31:47,010 --> 00:31:50,513
In the end, your class lost one student.

560
00:31:50,580 --> 00:31:53,850
You failed to get a good rating.
So I guess you're fired now.

561
00:31:54,751 --> 00:31:56,519
Don't say things like that.

562
00:31:56,586 --> 00:32:00,256
Try to persuade Yuu
to not quit our school!

563
00:32:00,323 --> 00:32:01,924
Unfortunately,

564
00:32:01,991 --> 00:32:05,728
we can't interfere with what the student
and guardian have decided.

565
00:32:05,795 --> 00:32:06,696
Right, Principal?

566
00:32:06,763 --> 00:32:08,965
Well, that's true.

567
00:32:09,032 --> 00:32:09,966
Let's go.

568
00:32:10,466 --> 00:32:12,168
What's up with that?

569
00:32:12,702 --> 00:32:16,806
Honestly, parents these days
are too soft on their kids, aren't they?

570
00:32:16,873 --> 00:32:19,375
Mr. Onizuka, you were unlucky.

571
00:32:19,442 --> 00:32:22,545
But I'm sure you will find
a good school somewhere.

572
00:32:22,612 --> 00:32:24,480
No, everyone,

573
00:32:24,547 --> 00:32:27,250
aren't you just pretending to be
sad while actually rejoicing?

574
00:32:27,316 --> 00:32:30,486
Could you stop talking like
I'm going to quit?

575
00:32:39,262 --> 00:32:43,699
Why is it that no matter where I go,
my career is always on a tightrope?

576
00:32:44,367 --> 00:32:46,169
ITO

577
00:32:51,841 --> 00:32:52,775
<i>Yes?</i>

578
00:32:55,211 --> 00:32:59,949
I am Eikichi Onizuka,
Ms. Yuu's homeroom teacher.

579
00:33:00,016 --> 00:33:01,084
<i>Yes?</i>

580
00:33:01,684 --> 00:33:03,986
Are you Ms. Yuu's mother?

581
00:33:04,687 --> 00:33:05,621
<i>Yes.</i>

582
00:33:06,856 --> 00:33:08,691
Could we talk for a moment?

583
00:33:10,293 --> 00:33:11,494
<i>Go ahead.</i>

584
00:33:12,895 --> 00:33:14,497
<i>Please speak from where you are.</i>

585
00:33:14,564 --> 00:33:17,667
Seriously, you're not going to let me in?

586
00:33:19,402 --> 00:33:23,106
About your daughter's withdrawal
from school, can't you reconsider?

587
00:33:23,172 --> 00:33:26,709
Can't you try to persuade her too,
as her mother?

588
00:33:26,776 --> 00:33:27,610
<i>I did try.</i>

589
00:33:27,677 --> 00:33:28,511
What?

590
00:33:29,278 --> 00:33:32,381
<i>But once she decides on something,</i>
<i>she won't listen, that girl.</i>

591
00:33:33,349 --> 00:33:35,885
Don't say that, please, I beg of you.

592
00:33:35,952 --> 00:33:40,389
She already got into our school,
so wasting a year would be a shame.

593
00:33:40,456 --> 00:33:42,592
Don't you think so too?

594
00:33:46,662 --> 00:33:47,964
Ma'am?

595
00:33:48,030 --> 00:33:50,032
<i>Are you saying I'm the one to blame?</i>

596
00:33:50,099 --> 00:33:53,002
No, that's not what I'm…

597
00:33:53,069 --> 00:33:57,340
<i>Didn't things turn out this way because</i>
<i>there's a problem with your school?</i>

598
00:33:58,374 --> 00:34:02,612
<i>My daughter told me a strange guy</i>
<i>became her homeroom teacher.</i>

599
00:34:02,678 --> 00:34:05,882
<i>This incident is your fault, isn't it?</i>

600
00:34:05,948 --> 00:34:08,384
<i>If so, I'll go protest at the school.</i>

601
00:34:08,451 --> 00:34:12,388
<i>Because of you, my daughter</i>
<i>has a deep wound in her heart…</i>

602
00:34:12,455 --> 00:34:14,090
Oh, enough.

603
00:34:14,690 --> 00:34:16,826
I have a dentist appointment,
so excuse me.

604
00:34:33,643 --> 00:34:34,677
<i>So,</i>

605
00:34:35,611 --> 00:34:39,982
it is very regrettable, but due
to personal circumstances, Ms. Yuu Ito

606
00:34:41,017 --> 00:34:42,985
will be leaving our school…

607
00:34:45,721 --> 00:34:46,756
Hey, Yuu.

608
00:34:47,490 --> 00:34:49,825
I can't accept this.

609
00:34:51,093 --> 00:34:52,962
I want us to create a Drill Team together,

610
00:34:53,629 --> 00:34:55,631
and I haven't even decided
your nickname yet.

611
00:34:56,699 --> 00:34:58,100
Could you please reconsider?

612
00:35:02,805 --> 00:35:05,308
Everyone, try to stop her too!

613
00:35:06,943 --> 00:35:11,747
You're in the same class,
separating like this is just too sad.

614
00:35:14,050 --> 00:35:16,986
Our class has 28 people,

615
00:35:17,053 --> 00:35:18,955
and it's a perfect number!

616
00:35:23,926 --> 00:35:25,494
Even if you say that…

617
00:35:26,996 --> 00:35:28,898
She's the one
who made the decision, right?

618
00:35:28,965 --> 00:35:31,667
I mean, this isn't an act too, is it?

619
00:35:31,734 --> 00:35:33,636
-What are you saying? No way…
-Everyone.

620
00:35:34,270 --> 00:35:37,306
It was only a short time,
but thank you for everything.

621
00:35:39,408 --> 00:35:40,610
Yuu!

622
00:35:42,812 --> 00:35:44,046
Yuu!

623
00:35:44,113 --> 00:35:46,048
Is this really okay with you?

624
00:35:46,115 --> 00:35:47,650
Oh, leave me alone.

625
00:35:49,986 --> 00:35:51,954
Ms. Kashiwabara, you say something too.

626
00:35:52,488 --> 00:35:53,456
Ms. Ito.

627
00:35:54,190 --> 00:35:55,224
Take care of yourself.

628
00:35:57,360 --> 00:35:58,394
Aren't you going to stop her?

629
00:35:58,461 --> 00:36:02,231
If she doesn't want to be at our school,
quitting is her choice.

630
00:36:02,298 --> 00:36:05,301
And at the next school she goes to, she
won't meet anyone like you, Mr. Onizuka.

631
00:36:06,335 --> 00:36:08,204
-What?
-Yes!

632
00:36:09,305 --> 00:36:11,140
It's your fault, Mr. Onizuka.

633
00:36:11,841 --> 00:36:14,243
Because you said you'd do
whatever you can for me.

634
00:36:16,479 --> 00:36:17,513
Right.

635
00:36:18,014 --> 00:36:20,449
I see. Just quit! Quit already!

636
00:36:21,017 --> 00:36:21,984
What?

637
00:36:22,051 --> 00:36:25,221
You're always trying
to run away. What's with that?

638
00:36:26,022 --> 00:36:29,892
From now on, whenever you're in trouble,
will you just get people to bail you out?

639
00:36:30,459 --> 00:36:32,395
Is it really fun doing things like that?

640
00:36:32,962 --> 00:36:34,430
Tell me, then.

641
00:36:36,198 --> 00:36:38,834
How will you get
good ratings from everyone?

642
00:36:39,869 --> 00:36:42,905
Well, about that…

643
00:36:42,972 --> 00:36:44,774
You can't answer, can you?

644
00:36:45,941 --> 00:36:48,377
Because you haven't been able
to get any yourself.

645
00:36:51,180 --> 00:36:54,583
Therefore, there's no choice but to reset!

646
00:36:55,851 --> 00:37:00,523
I don't want them to hate me more,
and I don't want to be made fun of either.

647
00:37:10,633 --> 00:37:11,701
What is it?

648
00:37:13,169 --> 00:37:17,340
I was wondering why you got so mad.
You even yelled, "Just quit!"

649
00:37:17,907 --> 00:37:19,308
I thought if I said that…

650
00:37:20,242 --> 00:37:22,878
She would get angry and not quit.

651
00:37:24,914 --> 00:37:27,550
Ms. Kashiwabara, why didn't you stop her?

652
00:37:28,084 --> 00:37:30,586
I'm sorry. But she reminded me of me.

653
00:37:31,387 --> 00:37:32,254
What?

654
00:37:32,321 --> 00:37:34,357
May of the first year of high school

655
00:37:34,423 --> 00:37:38,461
is when you feel anxious about whether you
can get along well in a new environment.

656
00:37:38,994 --> 00:37:41,397
And when I couldn't fit in with everyone,

657
00:37:41,464 --> 00:37:44,734
I also thought countless times
that I wanted to reset and start over.

658
00:37:49,638 --> 00:37:52,241
SEISHIN HIGH SCHOOL

659
00:38:01,183 --> 00:38:02,952
Don't mess around, Yuukichi!

660
00:38:03,552 --> 00:38:04,820
The Drill Team is the first team

661
00:38:04,887 --> 00:38:07,490
I joined throughout
middle and high school.

662
00:38:07,556 --> 00:38:11,327
Because through it, even someone like me
can interact with people,

663
00:38:11,394 --> 00:38:15,564
so when you suggested doing a Drill Team,
I thought you were seriously amazing.

664
00:38:16,232 --> 00:38:17,967
So what is this?

665
00:38:18,033 --> 00:38:20,770
Tell you what,
even if you go to another school,

666
00:38:20,836 --> 00:38:22,872
I'm going to keep up the Drill Team.

667
00:38:23,506 --> 00:38:26,442
I'll be the leader and gather five people…

668
00:38:26,509 --> 00:38:30,179
No, I'll make it
the biggest team in school!

669
00:38:30,246 --> 00:38:33,949
Chest out, swing your hands and feet wide,
a smile on your face.

670
00:38:37,853 --> 00:38:38,854
Yuu!

671
00:38:38,921 --> 00:38:41,190
Now that I've reached this age,

672
00:38:41,257 --> 00:38:43,759
I have a ton of things
I want to reset too,

673
00:38:44,693 --> 00:38:47,630
but I can't just erase what I've done.

674
00:38:48,264 --> 00:38:51,600
Even if you fail, even if you regret it,
you just have to keep going.

675
00:38:52,368 --> 00:38:53,402
I mean,

676
00:38:53,469 --> 00:38:56,705
don't try to reset
the hard work you put in so far.

677
00:38:57,940 --> 00:39:00,709
Even if it was embarrassing,
how can you hate yourself

678
00:39:01,410 --> 00:39:03,479
when you worked so desperately hard?

679
00:39:14,957 --> 00:39:16,892
Ms. Kashiwabara, won't you join us too?

680
00:39:16,959 --> 00:39:17,960
I'll pass.

681
00:39:18,027 --> 00:39:20,930
It's fine. Even if you're bad at it,
I'll teach you.

682
00:39:24,900 --> 00:39:26,035
Hey…

683
00:39:26,101 --> 00:39:27,770
Let's do the Hero pose.

684
00:39:29,405 --> 00:39:31,774
Hero pose! Sleep pose! Hero pose!

685
00:39:31,841 --> 00:39:33,676
Ms. Kashiwabara, you're super good!

686
00:39:33,742 --> 00:39:35,244
This kind of stuff is easy.

687
00:39:35,311 --> 00:39:36,846
Hero pose! Sleep pose!

688
00:39:37,413 --> 00:39:38,681
Can I join too?

689
00:39:38,747 --> 00:39:40,749
Oh, Ryunosuke! Come here!

690
00:39:40,816 --> 00:39:42,284
Hero pose! Sleep pose!

691
00:39:42,351 --> 00:39:44,019
Turn around!

692
00:39:55,130 --> 00:39:56,999
Onicchi, what are you doing?

693
00:39:57,066 --> 00:39:59,502
-Masaru, you get in here too, come on.
-What?

694
00:39:59,568 --> 00:40:01,403
It's more fun with a large group.

695
00:40:01,470 --> 00:40:03,138
-What are you doing?
-Just come on!

696
00:40:03,205 --> 00:40:04,907
I'm on a delivery right now.

697
00:40:05,574 --> 00:40:07,510
-Turn around!
-Turn?

698
00:40:08,677 --> 00:40:11,413
Turn? Is this some kind of penalty?

699
00:40:16,919 --> 00:40:18,921
Yuu, come on.

700
00:40:19,421 --> 00:40:20,456
You too.

701
00:40:56,859 --> 00:40:57,893
Ken-Ken!

702
00:41:00,596 --> 00:41:02,064
Hero pose! Sleep pose!

703
00:41:02,131 --> 00:41:03,499
Mr. Onizuka, I'm sorry.

704
00:41:03,566 --> 00:41:04,867
I'm begging you.

705
00:41:04,934 --> 00:41:07,570
Don't say you're quitting anymore.

706
00:41:12,608 --> 00:41:13,542
Hero pose!

707
00:41:13,609 --> 00:41:14,777
Sorry, Kenta.

708
00:41:14,843 --> 00:41:16,245
It's fine, Yuukichi.

709
00:41:16,312 --> 00:41:18,480
Hey, what's with that nickname?

710
00:41:18,547 --> 00:41:21,917
That's how I see you. It sounds
cheerful and similar to Onicchi.

711
00:41:21,984 --> 00:41:24,086
Yuukichi and Eikichi, huh?

712
00:41:25,054 --> 00:41:27,222
Hang on… Stop it!

713
00:41:28,057 --> 00:41:29,725
I don't get it.

714
00:41:29,792 --> 00:41:31,894
Eikichi, I have to make my delivery…

715
00:41:33,395 --> 00:41:34,296
Oh!

716
00:41:34,363 --> 00:41:36,899
That shocked me.
What's the matter, Ms. Kashiwabara?

717
00:41:36,966 --> 00:41:39,201
Sorry to rain on your parade, but…

718
00:41:39,268 --> 00:41:42,905
once a withdrawal notice is submitted,
you can't return to school anymore.

719
00:41:42,972 --> 00:41:44,406
What? No way!

720
00:41:44,473 --> 00:41:46,408
What should I do?

721
00:41:46,475 --> 00:41:47,876
Well…

722
00:41:47,943 --> 00:41:49,778
No worries, you are okay.

723
00:41:49,845 --> 00:41:51,280
Why?

724
00:41:52,147 --> 00:41:54,416
Because I haven't reported to my boss yet.

725
00:41:55,117 --> 00:41:56,218
I was holding on to it.

726
00:41:56,285 --> 00:41:59,054
You're the man, Ryunosuke!

727
00:41:59,121 --> 00:41:59,955
All right.

728
00:42:00,456 --> 00:42:01,590
Come on, Yuu!

729
00:42:15,004 --> 00:42:17,139
Hero pose! Sleep pose!

730
00:42:17,206 --> 00:42:20,876
Hero pose! Sleep pose! Stretch!

731
00:42:23,412 --> 00:42:24,713
Everyone,

732
00:42:25,814 --> 00:42:27,883
I'm sorry for causing such a fuss.

733
00:42:30,285 --> 00:42:34,223
If possible, could you let me be
your classmate once again?

734
00:42:35,090 --> 00:42:36,191
Please.

735
00:42:39,895 --> 00:42:42,431
From now on,
no matter how much I'm made fun of,

736
00:42:43,165 --> 00:42:47,236
I'll work hard so that
the Drill Team will be recognized.

737
00:42:51,640 --> 00:42:53,676
One more thing,

738
00:42:55,044 --> 00:42:57,146
Ken-Ken gave me a nickname.

739
00:42:57,212 --> 00:42:59,848
Yuukichi. So call me that, please.

740
00:43:10,592 --> 00:43:11,627
Mr. Nakamaru.

741
00:43:11,694 --> 00:43:13,062
Look at this.

742
00:43:13,128 --> 00:43:16,298
I got one more good rating!

743
00:43:16,365 --> 00:43:18,634
Can you read it? Need glasses?

744
00:43:18,701 --> 00:43:19,735
Shut up!

745
00:43:20,803 --> 00:43:23,005
As per our promise, don't fire me, okay?

746
00:43:23,072 --> 00:43:24,306
Shut up. Go over there.

747
00:43:24,373 --> 00:43:28,210
If possible, I'd like a bonus too.
My wife would be happy.

748
00:43:28,277 --> 00:43:29,511
Let go.

749
00:43:32,514 --> 00:43:33,615
Oh, right.

750
00:43:33,682 --> 00:43:34,516
Everyone.

751
00:43:34,583 --> 00:43:36,485
I've made you worry,

752
00:43:36,552 --> 00:43:38,921
but I, Eikichi Onizuka,
will keep believing in myself

753
00:43:38,987 --> 00:43:41,256
and raise my rating higher and higher,

754
00:43:41,323 --> 00:43:43,092
so look forward to it!

755
00:43:50,966 --> 00:43:52,935
CLASS 1-B

756
00:43:53,502 --> 00:43:55,904
Hey, I was thinking
it might be cool to do this.

757
00:43:55,971 --> 00:43:58,640
Oh, that's good. Feels so original!

758
00:43:58,707 --> 00:44:00,109
Yes!

759
00:44:04,913 --> 00:44:05,881
Oh…

760
00:44:09,051 --> 00:44:11,787
"Let's act as if Onizuka doesn't exist."

761
00:44:12,454 --> 00:44:14,623
I've been wondering
about this for a while…

762
00:44:15,190 --> 00:44:16,892
Who is the one doing this?

763
00:44:16,959 --> 00:44:17,926
Who knows.

764
00:44:39,515 --> 00:44:43,051
All right, I'm starting the class.
Come on, everyone. Take your seats.

765
00:44:47,990 --> 00:44:52,227
Everyone, let's have another
great school day!

766
00:44:53,729 --> 00:44:55,430
<i>Operation Confession is a go!</i>

767
00:44:55,497 --> 00:44:56,965
<i>Being glared at is creeping her out.</i>

768
00:44:57,032 --> 00:44:58,567
You like her, right?

769
00:44:58,634 --> 00:45:00,869
The only thing you need is courage.

770
00:45:00,936 --> 00:45:04,206
<i>It's problematic for a teacher</i>
<i>to meddle in student romances!</i>

771
00:45:04,273 --> 00:45:08,076
I won't forgive anyone who makes fun
of his feelings and hurts him.

772
00:45:08,143 --> 00:45:10,112
<i>Why haven't you gotten it</i>
<i>through your head yet?</i>

773
00:45:10,179 --> 00:45:13,682
Everything you say and do
is problematic in this era!

774
00:45:13,749 --> 00:45:14,950
Stop it!

775
00:45:15,017 --> 00:45:16,652
-It's so cold!
-Stop it!

776
00:45:16,718 --> 00:45:18,253
Don't spray me!

777
00:45:18,320 --> 00:45:19,688
<i>I really loved her.</i>

778
00:45:19,755 --> 00:45:23,091
Ayumu, stop! Don't do anything stupid!

779
00:45:23,158 --> 00:45:26,094
It's because he wants
to save everyone in the world!

780
00:45:26,161 --> 00:45:27,129
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

